<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Privacy policy | Lumière Archive</title>
    <style>
      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: #faf8f4;
        color: #25231f;
        font:
          17px/1.7 system-ui,
          sans-serif;
      }
      main {
        max-width: 780px;
        margin: auto;
        padding: 48px 24px;
      }
      h1,
      h2 {
        line-height: 1.25;
      }
      h1 {
        font-size: 2.4rem;
      }
      h2 {
        margin-top: 2rem;
        font-size: 1.3rem;
      }
      a {
        color: #685020;
      }
      aside {
        padding: 16px;
        border: 1px solid #b48b48;
        background: #fff3d6;
      }
      footer {
        margin-top: 40px;
        border-top: 1px solid #ccc;
        padding-top: 20px;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <%= render "shared/love_wins_band" %>
    <main>
      <aside>
        <strong>Draft — pending operator confirmation.</strong> Replace the
        bracketed operator and contact details and confirm the practices
        described here before publishing or submitting to Meta.
      </aside>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p>Last updated: October 8, 2026</p>
      <p>
        Lumière Archive (also known as Hedonism Bot) is a photography archive
        and gallery management application operated by
        <strong>Love Wins Media, Inc.</strong> (“we”, “us”). This policy
        explains how we handle information when you visit a gallery, upload
        photographs, or use Facebook Login. Contact us at
        <strong>[PRIVACY CONTACT EMAIL]</strong>.
      </p>
      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Facebook Login:</strong> When you sign in, we receive your
          app-scoped Facebook user ID, name, first and last name, and email
          address when available and authorized. We store the profile response,
          access token, and the time the token was received. Our current login
          requests the public_profile and email permissions. We do not receive
          your Facebook password.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Account and administration:</strong> We store account
          identifiers, sign-in session information, and permissions linking
          administrators to photographers and galleries. Signing in can create
          an account record even if you have not been granted administrator
          access.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Photographs and related information:</strong> We process
          uploaded original files, previews, album details, captions, and
          embedded image metadata, which may include capture times, camera
          information, and geographic coordinates when present. Photographs may
          depict people who do not have an account.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Image analysis:</strong> Our processing workers can generate
          descriptions and visual feature vectors, detect faces, create face
          crops and numerical facial representations (embeddings), and group
          similar faces across photographs. Facial representations may qualify
          as biometric data under applicable law. These results can be
          inaccurate.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Technical information:</strong> We process IP addresses,
          browser information, request and error logs, page URLs, and diagnostic
          details to operate, troubleshoot, and protect the service. Error
          reports may be associated with a signed-in user's internal identifier
          and gallery.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Requests:</strong> If you contact us, we process the
          information you provide to answer your request and verify that it
          relates to you.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <h2>How we use information</h2>
      <p>
        We use information to authenticate users, determine administrator
        access, store and display photographs, organize and search the archive,
        generate captions and face groupings, diagnose failures, protect the
        service, and respond to privacy requests. Facebook account information
        is used for sign-in and account administration. We do not use Facebook
        Login information to train machine-learning models. Photo analysis
        operates on uploaded photographs.
      </p>
      <h2>When information is shared</h2>
      <p>
        Photographs and associated gallery content are visible to people who can
        access the gallery, including the public where content is publicly
        available. Photographers and authorized administrators can manage
        content in their galleries. Please consider the privacy of people
        pictured before uploading or publishing photographs.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use service providers for hosting, databases, file storage,
        background processing, and operational support. The application supports
        Heroku hosting and Bucketeer/Amazon S3-compatible storage, including
        optional archive storage. When administrator SMS notifications are
        enabled, a new user's name is sent through Twilio to the administrator.
        Pages that load Google Fonts send ordinary web requests, including an IP
        address and browser information, to Google.
      </p>
      <p>
        Facebook processes information when you use Facebook Login under
        <a href="https://www.facebook.com/privacy/policy/"
          >Meta's Privacy Policy</a
        >. We may disclose information when legally required or necessary to
        protect rights, security, or safety. We do not sell personal information
        or share it for cross-context behavioral advertising.
      </p>
      <h2>Cookies and browser storage</h2>
      <p>
        We use session cookies to maintain sign-in and support security.
        Blocking or clearing these cookies may prevent sign-in or end your
        session. Facebook and other external services may use their own cookies
        when you interact with them.
      </p>
      <h2>Retention and security</h2>
      <p>
        We retain account information while needed to provide and administer
        access, and photographs and derived information while needed for the
        archive. We delete information when it is no longer needed or in
        response to a valid deletion request, subject to applicable legal
        obligations. Restricted backup copies may remain until they expire under
        the backup lifecycle. Where information must be retained for a legal
        obligation or dispute, we limit its use to that purpose.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use measures designed to protect information, including HTTPS,
        authenticated administrator access, and gallery access controls. No
        system can guarantee absolute security. Our providers may process
        information in countries other than yours; applicable transfer
        safeguards are used where required by law.
      </p>
      <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
      <p>
        You may request access, correction, or deletion of your personal
        information by contacting <strong>[PRIVACY CONTACT EMAIL]</strong>.
        Depending on your location, you may also have rights to portability,
        restriction, objection, withdrawal of consent, and a complaint to a
        privacy regulator. Where applicable, we process information to provide
        requested services, pursue legitimate interests in operating and
        securing the archive, meet legal obligations, or with consent where
        required. Withdrawal of consent does not affect processing already
        lawfully performed.
      </p>
      <p>
        To remove account information, Facebook data, photographs depicting you,
        or associated facial representations, follow our
        <a href="/data-deletion.html">data-deletion instructions</a>. You do not
        need to sign in to make a request. Removing this app in Facebook stops
        future access through that connection but does not itself erase
        information already stored by us.
      </p>
      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        The administrator service is intended for adults. If you believe a child
        has provided account information or a photograph of a child should be
        removed, contact us using the details above.
      </p>
      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        We will post changes on this page and update the date above. For
        material changes, we will provide additional notice where required.
        Privacy questions and requests may be sent to
        <strong>Love Wins Media, Inc.</strong> at
        <strong>[PRIVACY CONTACT EMAIL]</strong>.
      </p>
      <footer>
        <a href="/privacy.html">Privacy policy</a> ·
        <a href="/data-deletion.html">Data deletion</a>
        <%= render "shared/love_wins_footer", align: "flex-start" %>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
